<script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"The Mystery of the Idol: Once, when Lord Parshwanath was standing in kaussagga meditation, Meghmali brought down a torrential downpour upon him. The water rose to the Lord's nose, but the Lord continued chanting the Navkar Mahamantra in the kaussagga posture. In an earlier life, the Lord had rescued a snake and a she-snake being burned in a fire lit by Kamath, and had given them a good rebirth by reciting the Navkar Mahamantra to them; they were then born in the heavens as the goddess Padmavati and the god Dharnendra. When they recall the affliction inflicted upon the Lord, Padmavati Devi lifts up her throne so that the Lord does not drown, and Dharnendra Dev forms a canopy over the Lord's head to stop the rain. Even after this ordeal, Meghmali sees that the Lord's kaussagga posture has not wavered even slightly, and he realizes that this is Lord Parsha; he repents, falls at the Lord's feet and begs forgiveness. In this idol, the Lord is shown in the kaussagga posture, Padmavati Devi is shown holding up the throne, Meghmali is shown begging forgiveness at his feet, and Dharnendra has formed the canopy of a thousand serpent hoods. Just as a lotus flower does not sink in water, symbolizing this, the Lord's idol is set upon a lotus throne. On either side of the parikar are five small idols each, representing the Lord's first ten disciples (Ganadharas). This idol, carved from a single stone, is considered miraculous.\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"article\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"prose-none space-y-4 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.85] text-ink\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Parshwanath 2 of 108 - Shri Sahastraphana Parshwanath\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Main Deity: In the temple (derasar) located at Gopipura, Subhash Chowk, Surat, Gujarat, the Main Deity is Lord Shri Shitalnath. In the underground shrine (bhoyaru) there i